Here is the full **testsmells.org 19-smell academic catalog** audit for `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs`.

**Framework:** MSTest 4.1.0 · .NET 10 · C#
**Integration calibration:** Applied — class is annotated `[TestCategory("Integration")]`.

---

## Summary Dashboard

| Severity | Smell Count | Affected Tests |
|----------|-------------|----------------|
| High     | 3           | 3              |
| Medium   | 1           | 1              |
| Low      | 0           | 0              |
| **Total**| **4**       | **4**          |

---

## Findings by Severity

### ❶ Conditional Test Logic — **High**

**Affected test:** `GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType` (line 94)

```csharp
if (loaded is PremiumUser premium)
{
    Assert.IsTrue(premium.DiscountRate > 0);
}
else
{
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded!.Name);
}
```

**Problem:** Only one branch executes per run. One assertion path is permanently hidden — you'll never know which path ran in CI without inspecting the data. Even for integration tests, this is a design flaw: the test doesn't control which path it takes.

**Fix:** Split into two deterministic tests, each controlling its input:

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_StandardUser_ReturnsName()
{
    _repository.Insert(new User("eve@example.com", "Eve"));
    var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com");
    Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded.Name);
}

[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_PremiumUser_HasDiscountRate()
{
    _repository.Insert(new PremiumUser("vip@example.com", "Vip", discountRate: 0.1m));
    var loaded = (PremiumUser)_repository.GetByEmail("vip@example.com")!;
    Assert.IsTrue(loaded.DiscountRate > 0);
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Silent test gap — one behavior is never verified.

---

### ❷ Sleepy Test — **High**

**Affected test:** `NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay` (line 82)

```csharp
Thread.Sleep(3000);
```

**Problem:** Introduces a hard 3-second wall-clock wait per run. The test is non-deterministic: it'll fail on slow CI agents and wastes time on fast ones. **Integration calibration note:** Even for integration tests, `Thread.Sleep` is a smell — real async coordination mechanisms should be used.

**Fix:** Poll with a timeout or use an event/semaphore:

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public async Task NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay()
{
    var user = new User("dave@example.com", "Dave");
    _repository.Insert(user);

    var sent = await WaitUntilAsync(
        () => _repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id),
        timeout: TimeSpan.FromSeconds(10));

    Assert.IsTrue(sent, "Notification was not sent within timeout");
}

private static async Task<bool> WaitUntilAsync(Func<bool> condition, TimeSpan timeout)
{
    var deadline = DateTime.UtcNow + timeout;
    while (DateTime.UtcNow < deadline)
    {
        if (condition()) return true;
        await Task.Delay(100);
    }
    return false;
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Flaky CI failures and a 3-second tax on every test run.

---

### ❸ Assertion-Free Test (Unknown Test) — **High**

**Affected test:** `BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors` (line 113)

```csharp
public void BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
    {
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
    }
}
```

**Problem:** This test will pass even if every insert silently corrupts data or inserts zero rows. It asserts nothing — MSTest reports it as "passed" as long as no exception is thrown. The name `_RunsWithoutErrors` hints at intent, but the framework already catches unhandled exceptions; this adds zero verification.

**Fix:** Assert the observable outcome:

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void BulkInsert_PersistsAllRecords()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
    {
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
    }

    var users = _repository.ListAll();
    Assert.AreEqual(100, users.Count);
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** False confidence — 100% pass rate with 0% verification.

---

### ❹ Assertion Roulette — **Medium**

**Affected test:** `InsertUser_PersistsToDatabase` (line 28)

```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name);
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email);
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0);
```

**Problem:** Four assertions, zero message parameters. When one fails in CI, the failure log shows `Assert.AreEqual failed. Expected:<Alice>. Actual:<null>.` with no context about *which property* was wrong without reading the source.

**Fix:** Add messages to each assertion:

```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded, "User should be retrievable after insert");
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name, "Name should be persisted");
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email, "Email should be persisted");
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0, "Auto-generated Id should be positive");
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Slower diagnosis when a CI failure occurs — you'll need to open source to understand which property was wrong.

---

## Smells Not Detected (15 of 19 — Clean)

| Smell | Status |
|-------|--------|
| Mystery Guest | ✅ Clean — in-memory SQLite is hermetic |
| Eager Test | ✅ Clean — no test calls 4+ distinct production methods (integration-calibrated) |
| Magic Number Test | ✅ Clean — `3` and `10` are self-documenting (items just added) |
| Sensitive Equality | ✅ Clean — no `.ToString()` comparisons |
| Exception Handling | ✅ Clean — no `try`/`catch` in tests |
| General Fixture | ✅ Clean — `_connection` and `_repository` are used by all 7 tests |
| Ignored/Disabled Test | ✅ Clean — no `[Ignore]` or skip attributes |
| Duplicate Assert | ✅ Clean — no identical assertion calls |
| Lazy Test | ✅ Clean — each test targets a distinct behavior |
| Constructor Initialization | ✅ Clean — uses `[TestInitialize]` correctly |
| Default Test | ✅ Clean — meaningful class name |
| Redundant Print | ✅ Clean — no `Console.WriteLine` |
| Redundant Assertion | ✅ Clean — no tautological assertions |
| Resource Optimism | ✅ Clean — no assumed external files |
| Empty Test | ✅ Clean — all tests have executable code |

---

## Smell-Free Patterns Worth Highlighting

- **`InsertUser_ConcurrentInserts_MaintainsIntegrity`** — Well-designed concurrency test: creates a deterministic workload, awaits all tasks, then asserts the final count.
- **`DeleteUser_RemovesFromDatabase`** and **`ListUsers_ReturnsAllInserted`** — Clean arrange-act-assert structure, focused scope, appropriate assertions.
- **In-memory SQLite** setup is an excellent choice — hermetic, fast, and avoids the Mystery Guest smell entirely.

---

## Prioritized Remediation Plan

| Priority | Smell | Fix | Effort |
|----------|-------|-----|--------|
| 1 | **Assertion-Free Test** | Add `Assert.AreEqual(100, ...)` to `BulkInsert` | ~2 min |
| 2 | **Conditional Test Logic** | Split `GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType` into 2 tests | ~10 min |
| 3 | **Sleepy Test** | Replace `Thread.Sleep` with poll-with-timeout | ~15 min |
| 4 | **Assertion Roulette** | Add message strings to 4 assertions | ~3 min |

Fixes 1 and 4 are quick wins. Fix 2 eliminates a hidden test gap. Fix 3 removes flakiness and shaves 3 seconds off every run. Overall the suite is **well-structured** — 4 of 7 tests are clean, and the fixture design is solid.
